WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.962
DENSE_RANK also gives tied values the same rank.

00:00:04.962 --> 00:00:07.307
But it does not leave gaps.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:13.832
If two employees tie for second, the next distinct salary gets rank three.

00:00:13.832 --> 00:00:18.442
This is often useful for grouping distinct ordered levels.

00:00:18.442 --> 00:00:22.972
Ranking functions differ mainly in how they handle ties.

00:00:22.972 --> 00:00:28.977
ROW_NUMBER forces a unique sequence, RANK leaves gaps after ties, and DENSE_RANK does not.

00:00:28.977 --> 00:00:35.527
Add deterministic tie-breakers when a unique order matters;

00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:40.453
otherwise two executions can choose different rows among tied values.
